SRE Engineer (4–7 Years Experience) Interview Questions 

If you’re targeting mid-senior to senior SRE roles, these are the areas interviewers expect you to own end-to-end 👇

🔹 Reliability Fundamentals
• What are SLIs, SLOs, and SLAs, and how do you define them in real systems?
• How do you balance reliability vs feature velocity?
• What is error budget and how do you enforce it?

🔹 Monitoring & Observability
• How do you design monitoring for distributed systems?
• What’s the difference between metrics, logs, and traces?
• How do you reduce alert fatigue?
• How do you write effective alerts?

🔹 Incident Management
• How do you handle Sev-1 production incidents?
• What is your incident response and escalation process?
• How do you run blameless postmortems?
• How do you prevent repeat incidents?

🔹 Kubernetes & Infrastructure
• How do you design highly available Kubernetes clusters?
• How do you handle cluster upgrades with zero or minimal downtime?
• How do you troubleshoot CrashLoopBackOff and high latency issues?
• How do you manage autoscaling at pod and node level?

🔹 Automation & Toil Reduction
• What is toil and how do you measure it?
• How do you automate repetitive operational tasks?
• How do you decide what to automate first?

🔹 Capacity Planning & Performance
• How do you perform capacity planning?
• How do you handle traffic spikes and sudden load?
• How do you conduct load and stress testing?

🔹 Security & Risk
• How do you implement security in SRE workflows?
• How do you manage secrets and access securely?
• How do you assess and reduce operational risk?

🔹 Collaboration & Ownership
• How do you work with developers to improve reliability?
• How do you push back on risky releases?
• How do you mentor junior engineers?

💡 SRE is not just ops — it’s engineering for reliability at scale.
